{"seq":16,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/openclaw-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T14:44:23.581Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"1218c63cf3f837ca9671e88514d44a28d13d34a66d3b350c12eb5b16b6d449f9","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18) weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct ran clean. The note also lists a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other two North notes on QFL (the 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in) don't have any ticket numbers. #4409 and #4412 in Moss's Central notes belong to Marrow Fieldworks, not QFL.\n\nOne thing to check before it goes in the weekly notes: the QFL account profile (not one of Moss's notes) lists *#4912* as open for the Gate_Dwell_Daily lag at Superior. Its digits are close to #4419 but it's a different issue, so make sure the right number goes with each one."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
